# How long a fight lasts, and what it costs.
#
#     build\RatnaBay.exe --script Docs\scripts\fight.rbs
#
# The question this exists to answer: are ordinary fights long enough for
# blocking, stagger and chill to ever be seen? Recorded fights ran about two
# seconds, which is not.
#
# Swings are separated by 'wait' rather than fired in a burst, because the
# weapon cooldown refuses anything faster and a refused swing is not a fight.

echo === a shallow room, tier 1 ===

descend 1 20789
noclip on
god on
room 1
wait 3

enemies
watch enemies

# Eight swings a second apart is roughly the rate a player actually manages.
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
enemies

echo === a deep room, tier 4 ===

surface
wait 0.5
descend 4 20789
noclip on
room 6
wait 3

# Deep rooms are where the levels have climbed, so this is where a fight should
# have grown long enough to have a shape.
enemies
assert enemies has Lv

face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
face
swing
wait 0.5
enemies

shot captures/fight-deep.png
quit
